"""Builds the new footer, connects the legal page and accessibility statement to the footer's links, and adds the owner-only preview.

Run it from the project folder, AFTER unzipping starscapes-footer-pages-19oct.zip into it:   python3 tools/add-footer-pages.py

What it does: it makes exact edits to eight files that already exist: the app, the footer, the company details, the legal pages' data, the page descriptions, the pages list, the legal page and the text page.
  src/App.jsx, src/components/Footer.jsx, src/data/company.js, src/data/legalPages.js, src/data/pageMeta.js, src/data/staticPages.js, src/pages/LegalPage.jsx, src/pages/StaticPage.jsx

How it keeps you safe:
  - It checks ALL 8 files first. If any is not exactly the way it expects, it changes NOTHING and says which.
  - Before changing a file it keeps a copy, ending .before-footer-pages.
  - It is safe to run twice: a file already done is left alone.
  - The new files (src/components/footer.css, src/pages/simpleMarkdown.jsx, src/pages/staticpage.css) come in the zip itself.
"""
